title: 'Jeff Bezos, 2015 letter to shareholders: most decisions are two-way doors, and a big organization slows itself by treating them as one-way.'
pid: 0a833b7e-76f4-4155-b662-90d550e58e86
body: |2-
  https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1018724/000119312516530910/d168744dex991.htm
  Type 1 decisions are "consequential and irreversible or nearly
  irreversible", to be made "methodically, carefully, slowly". Type 2
  "can and should be made quickly by high judgment individuals or
  small groups". Using the heavy process for both yields "slowness,
  unthoughtful risk aversion". Read in the primary text.
